# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Raw/cached data — large, re-downloadable via scripts/01_fetch_data.py.
# results/ (metrics + figures) is committed on purpose: the demo notebook
# and slides must work offline, without Colab or network, on talk day.
data/raw/
data/cache/

# The only result file excluded from that rule: 33 MB even at zstd
# compression, over GitHub's warning threshold, and re-generated every time
# scripts/02_exp_mtg.py runs. scripts/02_exp_mtg.py writes a small (~8 MB)
# committed slice — exp_mtg_demo_slice.parquet — alongside it in the same
# run, which is what notebooks/demo.ipynb and scripts/06_make_figures.py
# actually read. Only scripts/04_exp_calibration.py needs the full file,
# and it already requires scripts/02 and 03 to have been run first.
results/exp_mtg_raw_predictions.parquet

# Same reason, larger: scripts/02b_exp_mtg_benchmark.py writes one row per
# (combo x origin x series x horizon step) across the whole preregistered
# grid — the shipped example config alone projects to ~10+ million rows,
# well past 02_exp_mtg.py's 33 MB. Regenerated by re-running 02b; nothing
# else in the repo reads it.
results/exp_mtg_benchmark_raw_predictions.parquet

# Editors, OS, caches
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.ipynb_checkpoints/
